<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina cuts soybean crop forecast.</title>
<headline>Argentina cuts soybean crop forecast.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina has reduced its estimate for 1996/97 soybean output to 13.5 million tonnes from a previous forecast of 13.9 million tonnes, Agriculture Secretariat said in its crop report Friday.</p>
<p>The Secretariat also reduced its forecast for sunflower seed output to 5.4 million tonnes from 5.6 million tonnes.</p>
<p>It cut its maize estimate to 14.28 million tonnes, from 14.35 million tonnes.</p>
<p>But it boosted its wheat output estimate to 15.8 million tonnes, from 15.5 million tonnes.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
